  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 802.36 Official of the municipality",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 802.36 “Official of the municipality” means an elected or appointed individual who, either individually or as a member of a duly-established local board, council, or commission, has oversight or other responsibility for land use activities in the municipality. The term includes the local health officer and members of the board of selectmen or city council, conservation commission, or planning board.\n\nSource. #10998, eff 1-1-16; ss by #14571, eff 5-15-26, EXPIRES: 5-15-36 (formerly Env-Wq 802.29)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq800.html"
